config EXAMPLES_HEALTH_MONITOR
	bool "Health monitor validation example"
	default n
	depends on HEALTH_MONITOR && !DISABLE_PTHREAD && !DISABLE_MQUEUE
	---help---
		Enable the health_monitor command for start, kick and stop through a
		worker thread, a periodic run cycle and numbered scenarios. Scenario 1
		tests two-thread ping-pong; scenarios 2..6 deliberately test missing
		kicks, semaphore deadlock, CPU starvation, sched_lock and unexpected
		exit. Scenario 7 uses a 10-second timeout, logs wall-clock and uptime
		changes, kicks after moving time forward/backward, then restores time
		and stops normally. No thread is monitored until a
		command explicitly starts monitoring.
		Scenarios 2..6 and expire deliberately trigger PANIC; reset behavior
		follows the board watchdog and panic configuration.
